Task 3: Deploy Camel Routes in OpenShift as Pods
Subtask 3.1: Build the Application
Build the Camel application:
mvn clean package -DskipTests
Verify the build was successful:
ls -la target/
Subtask 3.2: Create OpenShift Deployment Configuration
Create a directory for OpenShift resources:
mkdir src/main/fabric8
Create a deployment configuration file:
nano src/main/fabric8/deployment.yml
Add the following deployment configuration:
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: camel-routes
  labels:
    app: camel-routes
    version: v1
spec:
  replicas: 2
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: camel-routes
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: camel-routes
        version: v1
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: camel-routes
        image: camel-routes:latest
        ports:
        - containerPort: 8080
          name: http
        - containerPort: 8778
          name: jolokia
        env:
        - name: JAVA_OPTIONS
          value: "-Xmx256m -Xms128m"
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: "256Mi"
            cpu: "100m"
          limits:
            memory: "512Mi"
            cpu: "500m"
        livenessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /actuator/health
            port: 8080
          initialDelaySeconds: 30
          periodSeconds: 10
        readinessProbe:
          httpGet:
            path: /actuator/health
            port: 8080
          initialDelaySeconds: 10
          periodSeconds: 5
