Task 4: Configure Scaling Policies for Camel Routes
Subtask 4.1: Create Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA)
First, ensure metrics server is available (usually pre-installed in OpenShift):
oc get pods -n openshift-monitoring | grep metrics
Create an HPA configuration file:
nano hpa-camel-routes.yml
Add the following HPA configuration:
apiVersion: autoscaling/v2
kind: HorizontalPodAutoscaler
metadata:
  name: camel-routes-hpa
  namespace: camel-routes-lab
spec:
  scaleTargetRef:
    apiVersion: apps/v1
    kind: Deployment
    name: camel-routes
  minReplicas: 2
  maxReplicas: 10
  metrics:
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: cpu
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 70
  - type: Resource
    resource:
      name: memory
      target:
        type: Utilization
        averageUtilization: 80
  behavior:
    scaleDown:
      stabilizationWindowSeconds: 300
      policies:
      - type: Percent
        value: 10
        periodSeconds: 60
    scaleUp:
      stabilizationWindowSeconds: 60
      policies:
      - type: Percent
        value: 50
        periodSeconds: 60
      - type: Pods
        value: 2
        periodSeconds: 60
      selectPolicy: Max
Apply the HPA configuration:
oc apply -f hpa-camel-routes.yml
Verify HPA creation:
oc get hpa
oc describe hpa camel-routes-hpa
